#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition title=\"Important\" type=\"danger\">\n"
"  The concepts in this guide are currently available only in the Python API. Equivalent functionality will be made available in the C API in a future release.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition title=\"Important\" type=\"danger\">\n"
"  Les concepts de ce guide ne sont actuellement disponibles que dans l'API Python. Des fonctionnalités équivalentes seront disponibles dans l'API C dans une prochaine version.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This guide explains how to transpile a [`FermionicCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit\") to a standard [`QuantumCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.QuantumCircuit). It continues with the same time evolution example from the [fermionic circuits guide](circuit#fermionic-circuit-explanation).\n"
msgstr "Ce guide explique comment transpiler un [`FermionicCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit\") en un [`QuantumCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.QuantumCircuit) standard. Il poursuit avec le même exemple d'évolution temporelle que le [guide des circuits fermioniques](circuit#fermionic-circuit-explanation).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Transpilation stages {#transpilation-stages}"
msgstr "Étapes de transpilation {#transpilation-stages}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "As explained in [`qiskit_fermions.transpiler`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler#module-qiskit_fermions.transpiler \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler\"), the preset pass managers in this project split the transpilation into the following stages:\n"
msgstr "Comme expliqué dans [`qiskit_fermions.transpiler`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler#module-qiskit_fermions.transpiler \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler\"), les gestionnaires de passes prédéfinis de ce projet divisent la transpilation en les étapes suivantes :\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Input** {#input}"
msgstr "**Entrée** {#input}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Converts the input circuit to a directed acyclic graph (DAG) data structure.\n"
msgstr "Convertit le circuit d'entrée en une structure de données de graphe orienté acyclique (DAG).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Optimization** {#optimization}"
msgstr "**Optimisation** {#optimization}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Keeps the circuit in fermionic space. These passes use fermionic structure and commutation relations while problem-aware knowledge remains fully available. [`F2FSynthesis`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-f-2-f-synthesis#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.F2FSynthesis \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.F2FSynthesis\") is the pass that Trotterizes an [`Evolution`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-evolution#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution\") gate here, with a product formula or with [`FermionicQDrift`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-synthesis-fermionic-q-drift#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicQDrift \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicQDrift\"), and [`QDriftTrotterization`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-q-drift-trotterization#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.QDriftTrotterization \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.QDriftTrotterization\") its occupation-aware variant; see [Optimization Passes](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes#qiskit-fermions-transpiler-passes-optimization) for the full set and [Synthesize an Evolution gate in fermionic space](fermionic-synthesis#fermionic-synthesis-explanation) for how a product formula is chosen.\n"
msgstr "Conserve le circuit dans l'espace fermionique. Ces passes utilisent la structure fermionique et les relations de commutation tandis que les connaissances propres au problème restent pleinement disponibles. [`F2FSynthesis`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-f-2-f-synthesis#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.F2FSynthesis \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.F2FSynthesis\") est la passe qui Trotterise ici une porte [`Evolution`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-evolution#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution\"), avec une formule de produit ou avec [`FermionicQDrift`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-synthesis-fermionic-q-drift#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicQDrift \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicQDrift\"), et [`QDriftTrotterization`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-q-drift-trotterization#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.QDriftTrotterization \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.QDriftTrotterization\") sa variante sensible à l'occupation ; consulte [Passes d'optimisation](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes#qiskit-fermions-transpiler-passes-optimization) pour l'ensemble complet et [Synthétiser une porte Evolution dans l'espace fermionique](fermionic-synthesis#fermionic-synthesis-explanation) pour savoir comment une formule de produit est choisie.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Layout** {#layout}"
msgstr "**Disposition** {#layout}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Maps fermionic mode registers to quantum registers. For occupation-basis mappings like Jordan-Wigner, each fermionic mode maps to a single qubit. This stage also supports more general mappings where the number of qubits differs from the number of fermionic modes.\n"
msgstr "Fait correspondre les registres de modes fermioniques à des registres quantiques. Pour les mappings en base d'occupation comme Jordan-Wigner, chaque mode fermionique correspond à un seul qubit. Cette étape prend aussi en charge des mappings plus généraux où le nombre de qubits diffère du nombre de modes fermioniques.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Synthesis** {#synthesis}"
msgstr "**Synthèse** {#synthesis}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Converts fermionic gates to qubit operations by using the chosen fermion-to-qubit mapping. [`FermionicGate`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-gate#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicGate \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicGate\") instances are transformed into sequences of standard quantum gates. A barrier is carried through onto every qubit of each register it touched, so it continues to separate the gates on either side of it during the qubit stage.\n"
msgstr "Convertit les portes fermioniques en opérations sur qubits en utilisant le mapping fermion-vers-qubit choisi. Les instances de [`FermionicGate`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-gate#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicGate \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicGate\") sont transformées en séquences de portes quantiques standard. Une barrière est reportée sur chaque qubit de chaque registre qu'elle touchait, de sorte qu'elle continue de séparer les portes de part et d'autre pendant l'étape sur les qubits.\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Qubit** {#qubit}"
msgstr "**Qubit** {#qubit}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Transpiles the resulting qubit circuit by using standard Qiskit methods, including optimization, layout, and routing for your target hardware.\n"
msgstr "Transpile le circuit de qubits obtenu en utilisant les méthodes standard de Qiskit, y compris l'optimisation, la disposition et le routage pour ton matériel cible.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Output** {#output}"
msgstr "**Sortie** {#output}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Converts the internal DAG data structure to the desired output format.\n"
msgstr "Convertit la structure de données DAG interne vers le format de sortie souhaité.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "A practical example: transpilation using Jordan-Wigner {#a-practical-example-transpilation-using-jordan-wigner}"
msgstr "Un exemple pratique : transpilation avec Jordan-Wigner {#a-practical-example-transpilation-using-jordan-wigner}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Use the preset pass manager to transpile your fermionic circuit with the Jordan-Wigner fermion-to-qubit mapping:\n"
msgstr "Utilise le gestionnaire de passes prédéfini pour transpiler ton circuit fermionique avec le mapping fermion-vers-qubit de Jordan-Wigner :\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Tabs group=\"tab\">\n"
"  <TabItem value=\"python\" label=\"Python\">\n"
msgstr ""
"<Tabs group=\"tab\">\n"
"  <TabItem value=\"python\" label=\"Python\">\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    ```python\n"
"    >>> from qiskit_fermions.circuit import FermionicCircuit\n"
"    >>> from qiskit_fermions.circuit.library import Evolution\n"
"    >>> from qiskit_fermions.operators import FermionOperator, cre, ann\n"
"    >>> from qiskit_fermions.transpiler.presets import generate_preset_jw_pass_manager\n"
"    >>>\n"
"    >>> # Create the same fermionic circuit from the previous guide\n"
"    >>> circuit = FermionicCircuit(4)\n"
"    >>> hamiltonian = FermionOperator.from_terms([\n"
"    ...     ([cre(0), ann(2)], 0.5),\n"
"    ...     ([cre(2), ann(0)], 0.5),\n"
"    ...     ([cre(1), ann(3)], 0.5),\n"
"    ...     ([cre(3), ann(1)], 0.5),\n"
"    ... ])\n"
"    >>> hamiltonian.groups = [0, 0, 1, 1]\n"
"    >>> evolution = Evolution(4, hamiltonian, time=1.0)\n"
"    >>> circuit.append(evolution, circuit.register)\n"
"    >>>\n"
"    >>> # Generate the Jordan-Wigner transpilation pipeline\n"
"    >>> pm = generate_preset_jw_pass_manager()\n"
"    >>>\n"
"    >>> # Transpile the fermionic circuit to a qubit circuit\n"
"    >>> qubit_circuit = pm.run(circuit)\n"
"    >>>\n"
"    >>> # The result is a standard QuantumCircuit\n"
"    >>> print(type(qubit_circuit))\n"
"    <class 'qiskit.circuit.quantumcircuit.QuantumCircuit'>\n"
"    ```\n"
"  </TabItem>\n"
msgstr ""

